Sara needs to earn a total of $30 + $20 + $20 = $70 to buy the jacket and shoes. She has already earned $5 x 4 = $20 from babysitting. She needs to earn an additional $70 - $20 = $50 from mowing the lawn. She earns $4 each time she mows the lawn, so she needs to mow the lawn $50 / $4 = 12.5 times. Since she cannot mow the lawn half a time, she needs to mow the lawn 13 times to earn enough money to buy the jacket and shoes.

Final answer: \boxed{13}
